1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,750
The sunlight hitting your face
right now is older than

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:04,660
human civilisation.

3
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:06,168
Not the trip here.

4
00:00:06,688 --> 00:00:09,758
Crossing a hundred and fifty
million kilometres of space

5
00:00:09,768 --> 00:00:11,768
only takes about eight minutes.

6
00:00:12,208 --> 00:00:14,308
The slow part happens inside the
Sun.

7
00:00:14,708 --> 00:00:17,968
Its energy is made in the core,
by nuclear fusion.

8
00:00:18,417 --> 00:00:21,547
But the inside of the Sun is so
dense that light

9
00:00:21,557 --> 00:00:23,257
can't travel in a straight line.

10
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:26,067
It's absorbed and given off
again and again,

11
00:00:26,707 --> 00:00:28,307
zigzagging in random directions.

12
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:32,120
Scientists estimate that energy
takes tens of thousands of

13
00:00:32,130 --> 00:00:32,930
years,

14
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:36,270
maybe more than a hundred
thousand, to reach the surface.

15
00:00:36,875 --> 00:00:39,905
So the energy in today's
sunshine set out before the
first

16
00:00:39,915 --> 00:00:40,715
farms,

17
00:00:40,975 --> 00:00:42,155
cities or writing.

18
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:43,882
Eight minutes to reach you.

19
00:00:44,282 --> 00:00:46,322
Tens of thousands of years to
get out.
